// Intrinsics of std/time on the native backends (decision 0094),
// implemented in std/llrt/xo_time.c, which only programs that use
// std/time compile; imported by std/native/llrt/tz.xo (the zone rules in
// Xo, decision 0193 step 5; decision 0198 deleted their C path).

/// The TZif data that may hold the zone with this name, in the order to
/// try them: from the program's zone data (host false: the TZif data of
/// each constant name, the whole embedded database, or with
/// --tzdata=system the host's), or from the host's database (host true,
/// as time.LoadLocation reads it: $ZONEINFO as a directory or a zip, then
/// the system directories; "Local" is /etc/localtime). Empty when there
/// is none.
fn tz_data(name: Str, host: Bool) -> List[Bytes]
/// The zone named name kept so far (tz.xo's parsed zone, its id in its
/// first word), or the empty list.
fn tz_find(name: Str) -> List[Int]
/// Keeps the parsed zone z under name, its id written to its first word,
/// and returns it; a zone kept under name first is returned instead (z
/// is dropped). The empty list when the table is full. The table holds z
/// shared between threads until exit.
fn tz_keep(name: Str, z: List[Int]) -> List[Int]
/// The wall clock in seconds since the Unix epoch (the time of a load,
/// for Go's cache).
fn tz_now() -> Int
/// The machine's zone name from the /etc/localtime link, or "Local".
fn tz_local_name() -> Str

